WEBVTT

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:55.550
Is Minami not coming today?

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.100
Whoa!

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:04.270
He's such a slacker. Yomogi, get a grip!

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.770
Get a grip!

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.690
Dude, why can't you focus?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.980
That's what I'd like to know.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.900
Whoa!

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:12.900
Wow.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.990
He fell again.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:16.240
Are you okay?

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.080
Sorry, but it's almost time for work.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.840
What's up?

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.470
Gauma, where's Minami?

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:38.760
Ah, she called saying
she had to go meet someone.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.970
...she's stood up a bunch of guys.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:45.440
Oh, I see. Okay.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.810
See ya.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.360
Such a slacker.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.190
Departing

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.190
Please Hold The Handrail

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.450
So, Minami's meeting someone, huh?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.870
It'd be weird if I asked about it.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.700
What Is This Thumping Heart?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.700
Episode 4

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:13.920
My impression of Kano?
Is that what this is about?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.470
Pretty much.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.470
Hmm.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.350
She was super serious
with practice and stuff.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:25.600
But everyone loved her
'cuz she was cheerful.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.810
Cheerful?

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.980
Yeah.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:30.110
I see.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.020
Hmm?

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.980
That's different than the Kano I knew.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.400
Really?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:41.700
Oh, and I think Kano picked out
the song for that recital.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.290
And yet...

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.950
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:51.750
No, it's fine. I wanted to meet you
to learn stuff like that.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.220
Hmm. Sorry I'm not much help.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.970
No, it's okay.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.720
Wait. I think Urita might have a video.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.600
Video?

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:06.770
Yeah. Of chorus practice
for the club records.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:11.060
I bet Kano's in it a bunch.
Want his number?

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.360
Is that okay?

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.320
Of course. Urita would be happy to help.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.910
Thank you.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.540
Hey. Are you going around
asking people about Kano?

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.210
Yeah. I've always been
a little curious, so...

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.670
I see. I'll let you know if I
think of something. Good luck.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.560
Hey, you okay? Feeling sick?

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.600
Was I that zoned out?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.770
By that look, I'd say you're in love.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.730
Huh?

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.820
You've been acting sneaky lately.
You like someone, don't you?

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.990
It's not like that.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:06.580
You like someone, don't you?

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.160
Maybe I do.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.330
Ooh!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.130
Gimme a break.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:16.800
But it's a wonderful thing.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.720
Even a granny like me went through
a season or two of love.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.680
I bet.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.970
Who's a granny?!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:26.510
Didn't you say it yourself?

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:32.350
Freshman, get with it and
make your move before it's too late.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.810
Too late...

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.270
Ask her out on a date.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:37.520
A date?!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.990
You're sick after all.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.400
Inamoto

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:42.440
Inamoto

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:42.480
Inamoto

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.910
Today

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.910
It's been so long, 

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.410
Huh? Wh-What's this?

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:54.250
What does it mean? Is this like... a date?

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:57.340
Hey, quit your mumbling over there.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:58.880
Y-You were here?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.960
Have been since morning.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.470
Oh, right. Yeah.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.760
Did you meet the chorus grad?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.510
Yeah.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.470
Alone?

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.850
Yeah.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.310
You sure have changed.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:17.020
I'm a big girl high-schooler now, Mom.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.820
Cut it out.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.780
Who made you change?

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.910
It's not from anyone's influence.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.080
Smirk much?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.040
It must be rough working
mornings and nights. Poor guy.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.800
Well, it's easy compared to
5,000 years ago.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.800
I can imagine.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:49.510
Yomogi, is your cold getting worse?

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.390
Shoot, I've gotta go.
Thanks for breakfast.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.190
You can skip training today.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.980
Crap, I'm gonna be late.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:07.320
How is that fair?

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.870
Hurry, hurry! Hurry, hurry!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.910
Uh, allow me to introduce

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:19.960
the exchange students
transferring to our school.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.210
No way.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.840
Seriously?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:29.390
Go figure. He's in our class.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:33.270
I'm hoping for a wonderful
experience in Japan.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:36.060
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:42.190
Thank you, Sizumu. For your seat,
just take the one behind Minami.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.740
Moving on, I have a few
announcements to make.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:47.860
Nice to meet you.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.320
Yeah. Nice to meet you.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:58.500
That wasn't just some coincidence, right?

00:07:58.500 --> 00:07:59.330
What?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.420
Why's your face red?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.500
Uh, it's my cold.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.970
Where is Dynazenon? You guys should know.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:08.840
Huh?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.970
Not here.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.550
It's hidden far away.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.760
But I just saw it flying.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:14.720
He saw.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.480
I was gonna be late!

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.690
You can't use it like that!

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.060
I'm not here to fight.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.860
I ask because I'm curious about you two.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:31.450
Seeing as how I'm an exchange student,
I hope we can all get along.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.790
That sure caught me off guard.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:38.040
His outfit?

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.040
What?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.460
He said he's not here to fight,
but shouldn't we tell Gauma?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:46.260
But you know he'd charge right in.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:47.540
No Trespassing

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:47.460
He might.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:50.930
Say what?! That's bullshit!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.050
"Charge!!"
"Full Throttle"
"Grand Opening"

00:08:54.470 --> 00:09:00.060
You guys used to get along with Gauma
5,000 years ago, right?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.690
Back then, maybe.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.480
This conversation...

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.310
Why?

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.740
Maybe you can work it out without <i>kaiju</i>.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.490
They'll appear even if we do.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.820
Do you guys make the <i>kaiju</i>?

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:19.750
No. They grow by people's wills.
The Eugenicists don't create <i>kaiju</i>.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:24.670
We just want to create a world
where <i>kaiju </i>are needed.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.880
You're not <i>kaiju </i>users, are you?

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.380
Hard to say.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:34.300
I don't think so,
but Gauma believes we are.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:38.220
What makes you think
you need to fight <i>kaiju</i>?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.190
Deep inside, maybe you just
want to fight them?

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.770
That's not it. We're just
doing what we can.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:48.280
Why are <i>kaiju </i>born?

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:54.820
People may seem free,
but everyone's bound by something.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:10:00.160
It's <i>kaiju </i>that frees them
from that something.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.580
Where the hell are you hiding?!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.580
It's Gauma.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.130
What's with his outfit?

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.130
Huh?

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.510
I'm not hiding.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:13.720
What are you plotting
by approaching these guys?!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.930
Can't a transfer student make friends?

00:10:16.930 --> 00:10:18.640
Friends, my ass!

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.140
I'll slug you in the kisser!

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.060
He dodged!

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.850
You gave it away.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:27.440
I'll slug you! I'll slug you so hard!

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.360
You little...!
You're asking for it, bastard!

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.070
What's this about?!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:36.530
Huh? Uh, I came to see someone.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.540
You're coming with us!

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.540
You've got all it wrong! Let go!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.000
Would you behave?!

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.000
Let go of me!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.040
Let go! I can explain myself!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.580
The hell was Sizumu thinking?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:52.550
He can hear <i>kaijus</i>' voices,
so perhaps he has a plan.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:56.220
Can I add the savory white custard?

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.220
Is that all?

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:07.810
It's a cold for sure. Stay home.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:12.030
No, I can't. Ugh, my head hurts.

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:15.780
Don't be silly! You want to
spread it to everyone?!

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:18.450
Mom, you're so loud!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.950
Were you okay after that?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:25.750
Yeah.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.290
They reported you?

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.960
Yeah, and I got fired from my job.

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:34.010
I got screwed. Next time,
I'll be more careful.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:35.590
Where's Yomogi?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:40.970
Oh, he's got a nasty cold.
Probably won't be coming for a while.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.930
Wouldn't it be bad if a <i>kaiju </i>came?

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.020
You totally want that.

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:49.900
Oh, Gauma. I need a day off next week.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.480
You have every day off!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.690
Yume, check up on Yomogi after school.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:59.490
Huh? What's the point if it's just a cold?

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:04.240
Yomogi's been slacking lately
like his heart isn't in it.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:06.410
How is that my problem?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:11.540
If you hadn't made him wait in the rain,
he wouldn't be sick.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:17.510
I found a <i>kaiju</i>.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:20.590
What a weird one. Strange power.

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:30.400
I haven't zoned out like this in a while.

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:34.860
Freshman, get with it and
make your move before it's too late.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.320
Ask her out on a date.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.030
Date...

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.870
Something is wrong with me.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:45.790
When she's like that,
it ain't easy for me.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:50.080
Here to visit?! How nice of you to come!

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:54.420
By the tone of her voice,
I bet it's just Gauma.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:02.340
Hmm? You're sleeping.
And here I bought all this stuff.

00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.480
You're up.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:10.770
Huh? What?

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.650
That's trippy.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:21.030
It's a very <i>kaiju</i>-like power.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.490
It's like it shifts dimensions.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.080
Whatever. Go for it, Mujina!

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.460
Instance Domination.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:36.250
Gauma said I should check up on you.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.710
I see.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.260
What are you looking at?

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:44.140
Huh? You have stuff you don't want seen?

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:46.050
Not really. No.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.640
I'm kidding.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.890
I didn't know you told jokes.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:56.400
Huh? Who do you think I am?
We only started talking recently.

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.820
True.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:04.320
I heard from Gauma that you couldn't
come to training the other day.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:05.370
Yeah.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.830
'Cuz you were meeting someone.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.120
Yeah. A chorus club grad.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.370
Chorus club?

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:15.000
Oh, for your sister.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:20.840
They knew a bit about her,
but it wasn't like they knew her well.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.130
I see.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:26.010
But they put me in touch
with someone. A guy.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.260
A guy?

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.560
Yeah.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:30.270
You okay?

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.310
Yeah. F-Fine.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:35.440
It's Gauma.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:36.360
<i>Kaiju?</i>

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:39.070
Yume! Come quick with Dyna Wing!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:40.820
Got it.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:44.200
I think... you're in no shape to help.

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:45.110
But--!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:47.910
Give me yours.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:49.540
Huh? Dyna Soldier?

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:55.920
Yeah. We gotta do everything we can.
Before it's too late.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:57.500
Too late...

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:05.590
Thanks. We'll have someone pilot it.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:07.510
Yeah. Be careful.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:09.220
Get some rest.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.110
You can eat that.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:31.660
Access Mode... Dyna Striker!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:35.120
Access Mode... Dyna Diver!

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:36.580
There they are.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:47.550
Eat this!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.140
That's not gonna work!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:00.110
Why'd it go through, dammit?!
Where's Yume?!

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:04.990
Gauma, Yomogi's too sick to fight.
I brought Dyna Soldier instead.

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:08.160
We can't combine without a pilot for it!

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.910
It's my time to shine!

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.240
Wh-When did you--?!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.450
Chise Asukagawa will pilot Dyna Soldier!

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.000
Okay! Go for it!

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.460
Hey! Who said it's up to you?!

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:24.210
Access Mode... Dyna Soldier!

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.840
I did it! I did it! I really did it!

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.100
She did it.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.350
What now?

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.310
Let's combine and fight!

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.480
Can you, Chise?

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:39.190
Yeah! If I think of it as a game!

00:16:42.900 --> 00:16:46.070
Hey! What happened to combining?!

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:48.490
I wish I could, but...!

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:50.990
Crush the little one, Mujina!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.910
Quit bossing me around!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.580
Hey, Chise! Look out!

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.920
Chise!

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.800
Thanks, Senpai.

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:10.590
Don't make me go to another memorial.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:17.720
Deep inside, maybe you just
want to fight them?

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.810
What makes you think
you need to fight <i>kaiju</i>?

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:24.190
That's what I'd like to know.

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:28.400
How is it, Minami?

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.700
Real ugly.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.570
Huh? I should come.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:33.740
Yeah. We might need you.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:37.080
Having said that, how do I get there?

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.410
It's not like I can borrow Mom's car.

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.750
Yomogi, hop in!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:52.930
We can only buy her so much time!

00:17:52.930 --> 00:17:54.930
Chise, let's switch!

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:57.560
I-I'd appreciate it!

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:08.150
Dyna Soldier Wing Combine!

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:12.150
Y-Yomo, are you okay?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.780
I-I'm far from okay!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.080
All right, let's combine!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.330
Right!

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:05.870
Combine Dragon Dynazenon!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.710
Dynazenon...

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.420
...Battle, Go!

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.260
Something Beam!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.100
Penetrator Gun!

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:27.440
Mujina, focus!

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.400
Your shouting doesn't help!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.490
Burst Missile Kick!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.170
Let's finish it!

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.580
--Right!
--Achoo!

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:07.640
Super Dragon Dyna Rex!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:13.820
Up you go! Heave ho!

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.570
Eat this!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.950
Blazing Inferno...

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:25.200
...Rex Roar!

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.170
Damn that Gauma!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.340
Good work.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.050
You, too.

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:41.390
Let's go.

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.650
I thought I was dead.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.280
Thank you!

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:04.830
You're a lifesaver, Yomo! I'll do my best
to train as your Dyna Soldier backup!

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:06.040
You don't have to.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:08.250
By next week, I'll...

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:10.120
No! I'll combine by tomorrow!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:14.750
Dynazenon... Can anyone pilot you?

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.920
What makes you so sure?

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.750
If you can do it, I can, too!

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.000
Want a ride?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.000
How rude.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.420
Huh?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.420
What?

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:27.890
Thanks for coming to get me.

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:32.150
I should've brought you along
from the start.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:35.020
Can I come along next time?

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.110
Next time?

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:39.700
When you go asking about your sister.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:43.280
Sure, but why?

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.950
I want to know more about you, too.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.710
Sorry. What was that?

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:54.000
Nothing.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.300
Stand! Bow!

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.050
Good morning.

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:07.970
Uh, don't forget that your second period
will be in the language lab today. Also--

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:07.970
Huh?

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:16.860
I guess I caught it.
